1. Technical Implementation Plan & Roadmap
Phase 0: Planning & Scope (Weeks 1–2)
* Tier Mapping Strategy: Formulate definitions for Tiers 1–4, capturing Neurotransmitter/synaptic dynamics, GWAS meta-analysis loci, Phenotype-mapped executive function SNPs, and Protective/modifier alleles.
* Target Scale: Establish an initial dataset of ≥5,000–10,000 curated SNP entries, engineered for scaling to 50,000+ via automated ingestion pipelines.
* Legal Mapping Goals: Rebutting claims of willful non-compliance, establishing Medically Determinable Impairment (MDI), automating Section 504 and ADA Title II accommodation triggers, structuring 42 U.S.C. § 1983 bad-faith arguments, and supporting SSI/SSDI Residual Functional Capacity (RFC) determinations.
* Security & Compliance Architecture: Implement Genetic Information Nondiscrimination Act (GINA) data isolation, enforce HIPAA compliance, incorporate NIST Post-Quantum Cryptography standards (ML-KEM/Kyber for key encapsulation and ML-DSA/Dilithium for signatures), build immutable audit logging, and design multi-factor consent flows.
Phase 1: Data Sourcing & Curation (Weeks 3–4)
* Public Catalogs Ingestion: Integrate data feeds from dbSNP, ClinVar, GWAS Catalog, PGC ADHD summary statistics, 1000 Genomes, gnomAD, PsychENCODE, and GTEx eQTL cortical datasets (specifically DLPFC, ACC, and Striatum).
* High-Priority Loci Targeting: Focus curation on COMT rs4680 (Val158Met), SLC6A2/NET1, BDNF rs6265 (Val66Met), SLC6A3/DAT1, DRD4 VNTR/rs1800955, SNAP25, ADGRL3, ST3GAL3, TIE1, PTPRF, MEF2C, and SORCS3.
* Phenotype & Legal Mapping: Map specific genomic variants directly to clinical psychometric indicators (e.g., Wisconsin Card Sorting Test, Continuous Performance Test, Stroop Task, working memory ceiling metrics) and systematically link these to statutory defense claims ("rebuts willfulness," "supports MDI," "triggers 504 extended time").
Phase 2: Database Schema & Security Architecture (Weeks 5–6)
* Database Schema: Implement relational and graph structures across primary tables: snpReferenceLibrary, geneticData, tokenizedSnpMap, snpPhenotypeMap, snpLegalClaimMap, polygenicScoreComponents, and auditLog.
* Encryption Standards: Enforce AES-256-GCM encryption at rest across all data layers. Apply NIST ML-KEM/Kyber KEM and ML-DSA/Dilithium digital signatures for tokenized genetic records. Maintain absolute logical and physical segregation between genetic datasets and FERPA educational records.
Phase 3: Ingestion Pipeline & Automation (Weeks 7–9)
* ETL Pipeline: Build end-to-end processing: VCF File Parsing → ANNOVAR/VEP Variant Annotation → TLMEM Functional Mapping → Legal Claim Graph Linking.
* Psychometric & Neuroimaging Validation: Automate cross-validation routines connecting genomic findings with ASRS/CADI diagnostic screeners and standard fMRI biological markers.
* Polygenic Score Calculation: Deploy an ADHD-PGS calculation engine featuring executive-function residualization models.
Phase 4: Integration into Platform Modules (Weeks 10–12)
* 504 Plan Builder: Deploy an automated mapping engine converting individual SNP risk profiles into specific classroom and testing accommodations.
* TLMEM Cascade: Operationalize the 5-tier analytical flow: SNP Variant → Neurochemical Impact → Neuroanatomical Alteration → Functional/Psychometric Limitation → Statutory Legal Claim.
* Gov-LLM Brief Generator: Automate context insertion of the complete biological-to-legal evidence cascade into draft court filings, including 42 U.S.C. § 1983 briefs, Younger abstraction exceptions, Monell liability claims, and SSA RFC applications.
Phase 5: Validation, Testing & Compliance (Weeks 13–15)
* Integrity & Security Audits: Conduct unit testing, boundary analysis, and full cryptographic validation of PQC signatures.
* Expert Review: Perform multidisciplinary clinical and legal reviews of generated legal exhibits and automated evidentiary reports.
* Accessibility & Performance: Ensure full adherence to WCAG 2.1 AA / 3.0 cognitive UI guidelines, maintaining edge query response times under 200ms.
Phase 6: Maintenance & Expansion (Ongoing)
* Continuous Updates: Execute quarterly GWAS summary statistic ingestion, process CC0 open-source community contributions, and publish sanitized, non-PII reference libraries.


