4. Architectural Overview & Deployment Guide
Overview
The TLMEM SNP Database provides a cryptographic, post-quantum secure pipeline connecting objective genomic variants to neurobiological impairments, functional psychometric limits, and statutory legal claims in administrative and federal education proceedings.
Database Setup & Migration
1. Provision a TiDB or MySQL instance configured with encrypted tablespaces.
2. Execute the ORM schema migrations for snpReferenceLibrary, tokenizedSnpMap, and auditLog.
3. Configure the NIST PQC cryptographic provider (oqsprovider / Liboqs) to enable ML-KEM-1024 key encapsulation and ML-DSA-8784 digital signatures on all tokenized genetic records.
4. Verify strict physical and logical boundary controls between GINA genetic data stores and FERPA educational logs.


